# Treat extensions as private by default.
#
# This directory is auto-discovered by the CLI at runtime, so any *.py
# file dropped in here becomes a subcommand group regardless of whether
# git tracks it. Most extensions an instructor writes will be course- or
# content-specific and shouldn't ship with the public repository, so the
# pattern below ignores everything except the files we want to track as
# worked examples.
#
# To promote a new extension to "tracked example", add another
# `!filename.py` exception below.

*.py
!__init__.py
!_example.py
!playbook.py
